<title>USA: U.S. copper service center shipments dip in Sept.</title>
<headline>U.S. copper service center shipments dip in Sept.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shipments from U.S. copper service centers in September dipped 0.9 percent below the August level, the Copper and Brass Servicenter Association reported.</p>
<p>In the first nine months of the year shipments were 2.3 percent below the comparable period in 1995.</p>
<p>Copper sheet, coil and strip continue to lead the way, up 9.9 percent in the first nine monts of 1996, but copper pipe and tube shipments were off 17.7 percent, and the second largest volume category, alloy rod and bar, were down 12.7 percent.</p>
<p>Stocks continue to be well below year ago levels in volume and price.</p>
<p>CBSA members felt October and November would be moderately good.</p>
<p>-- New York Commodities 212-859-1646</p>
</text>
